      "writtenOn": "2026-10-13T17:43:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `task_set_event()`, `atomic_or(\u0026data-\u003eevent_mask, event)` and `k_poll_signal_raise(\u0026data-\u003enew_event, 0)` are not atomic together:\n1. If a second caller runs `atomic_or()` and is preempted before `k_poll_signal_raise()`, the waking task can reset `new_event` and consume both events via `atomic_set(\u0026data-\u003eevent_mask, 0)`, after which the preempted caller raises `new_event` with `event_mask \u003d\u003d 0`.\n2. Callers can also clear bits directly via `task_get_event_bitmap()` (or call `task_set_event(id, 0)`), leaving `new_event` signaled with `event_mask \u003d\u003d 0`.\n\nMigrating `task_ctx_base_data` to `struct k_event` would avoid this, would be a worthwhile followup.",
      "parentUuid": "6d04a8c1_a84315c9",
